CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ const reference paren-init binds to s: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ scalar reference paren-init binds to i: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ non-const reference paren-init aliases s: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ const reference sees the update through alias: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^(ERROR|error): .*declared as reference but is not initialized
--
N5008 [dcl.init.ref], [dcl.init]/16: reference direct-initialization with
parentheses (T &r(init)) binds the reference like T &r = init.  CBMC previously
reported such a reference as uninitialized (the parenthesized initializer was
stored as init_args and not attached).  This is the layer behind the
replace_symbol.cpp goto-cc cascade (`const exprt &const_dest(dest);`).
assertion.5 FAILURE proves non-vacuity.
